<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="lt4-combining-like-terms">
<title>Learning Target 4: Combining Like Terms</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
<li>I can simplify algebraic expressions by combining like terms.</li>
</ul>
</objectives>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-1" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 1</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>9x - 3(4 - 2x) + 5</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Multiply <m>4</m> and <m>-2x</m> by <m>-3</m>:<md>9x - 12 + 6x + 5</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>9x + 6x - 12 + 5</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>15x - 7</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-2" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 2</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>6 + 4x - (2x + 9)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the negative sign to both terms inside the parentheses:<md>6 + 4x - 2x - 9</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>4x - 2x + 6 - 9</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>2x - 3</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-3" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 3</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>5(2x - 1) - 2(3x - 4)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the <m>5</m> and the <m>-2</m>:<md>10x - 5 - 6x + 8</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>10x - 6x - 5 + 8</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>4x + 3</md></p>
<p>Be careful with the second group. The <m>-2</m> multiplies both terms, so <m>-2 \cdot (-4) = 8</m>, not <m>-8</m>.</p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-4" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 4</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>3x^2 + 5x - 2 + 4(x^2 - 2x + 3)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the <m>4</m>:<md>3x^2 + 5x - 2 + 4x^2 - 8x + 12</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>3x^2 + 4x^2 + 5x - 8x - 2 + 12</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>7x^2 - 3x + 10</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-5" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 5</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>2x^2 - x + 7 - (5x^2 - 4x + 1)</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the negative sign to all three terms inside the parentheses:<md>2x^2 - x + 7 - 5x^2 + 4x - 1</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>2x^2 - 5x^2 - x + 4x + 7 - 1</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>-3x^2 + 3x + 6</md></p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise xml:id="lt4-simplify-6" workspace="3.25in">
<title>Problem 6</title>
<statement>
<p>Simplify the expression using any method you like. Show your work or explain your reasoning.</p>
<p><md>7 - 2(x^2 + 3x) + 6x - x^2</md></p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p>Distribute the <m>-2</m>:<md>7 - 2x^2 - 6x + 6x - x^2</md></p>
<p>Group the like terms together:<md>-2x^2 - x^2 - 6x + 6x + 7</md></p>
<p>Combine the like terms:<md>-3x^2 + 7</md></p>
<p>The <m>x</m> terms combine to <m>-6x + 6x = 0</m>, so there is no <m>x</m> term left in the simplified expression.</p>
</answer>
</exercise>
</page>

</worksheet>
